{"id": "tea:astadhyayi:1.2.27", "source": "src:astadhyayi", "location": {"ref": "1.2.27"}, "paraphrase": "A vowel whose duration is that of u, ū or u3 is called short, long or prolated (hrasva, dīrgha, pluta).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:matra"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "disagreements": []}, "notes": "Phase-B spot check: wording/locator matched against the local GRETIL/DCS e-text in sources_raw/ (not a formal Phase-C sourcing check).", "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-28", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["local text lookup 1.2.27"], "evidence": ["text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/mixed/gretil_devanAgarI/1_sanskr/6_sastra/1_gram/panini_astadhyayi.md (GRETIL)"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "A 1.2.27 'ūkālo 'j jhrasvadīrghaplutaḥ'. Paraphrase agrees.", "by": "sourcing:U02-brahmana-vedanga"}]}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:astadhyayi:1.2.29-31", "source": "src:astadhyayi", "location": {"ref": "1.2.29-31"}, "paraphrase": "A vowel pronounced high is udātta, one pronounced low is anudātta, and one combining both is svarita.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:svara"], "concepts": ["cpt:power-of-accent"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "disagreements": []}, "notes": "Phase-B spot check: wording/locator matched against the local GRETIL/DCS e-text in sources_raw/ (not a formal Phase-C sourcing check).", "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-28", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["local text lookup 1.2.29-31"], "evidence": ["text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/mixed/gretil_devanAgarI/1_sanskr/6_sastra/1_gram/panini_astadhyayi.md (GRETIL)"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "A 1.2.29–31 'uccair udāttaḥ | nīcair anudāttaḥ | samāhāraḥ svaritaḥ'. Paraphrase agrees.", "by": "sourcing:U02-brahmana-vedanga"}]}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:astadhyayi:1.2.45", "source": "src:astadhyayi", "location": {"ref": "1.2.45"}, "paraphrase": "A meaningful form that is not a verbal root, not an affix and not ending in an affix is a nominal stem (prātipadika).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:pada"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "disagreements": []}, "notes": "Phase-B spot check: wording/locator matched against the local GRETIL/DCS e-text in sources_raw/ (not a formal Phase-C sourcing check).", "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-28", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["local text lookup 1.2.45"], "evidence": ["text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/mixed/gretil_devanAgarI/1_sanskr/6_sastra/1_gram/panini_astadhyayi.md (GRETIL)"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "A 1.2.45 'arthavad adhātur apratyayaḥ prātipadikam'. Paraphrase agrees.", "by": "sourcing:U02-brahmana-vedanga"}]}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:astadhyayi:1.3.1", "source": "src:astadhyayi", "location": {"ref": "1.3.1"}, "paraphrase": "The items beginning with bhū are verbal roots (dhātu).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:dhatu"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "disagreements": []}, "notes": "Phase-B spot check: wording/locator matched against the local GRETIL/DCS e-text in sources_raw/ (not a formal Phase-C sourcing check).", "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-28", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["local text lookup 1.3.1"], "evidence": ["text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/mixed/gretil_devanAgarI/1_sanskr/6_sastra/1_gram/panini_astadhyayi.md (GRETIL)"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "A 1.3.1 'bhūvādayo dhātavaḥ'. Paraphrase agrees.", "by": "sourcing:U02-brahmana-vedanga"}]}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:astadhyayi:1.4.14", "source": "src:astadhyayi", "location": {"ref": "1.4.14"}, "paraphrase": "What ends in a nominal ending (sup) or a verbal ending (tiṅ) is a word (pada).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:pada"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-classes-of-words"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "disagreements": []}, "notes": "Phase-B spot check: wording/locator matched against the local GRETIL/DCS e-text in sources_raw/ (not a formal Phase-C sourcing check).", "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-28", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["local text lookup 1.4.14"], "evidence": ["text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/mixed/gretil_devanAgarI/1_sanskr/6_sastra/1_gram/panini_astadhyayi.md (GRETIL)"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "A 1.4.14 'suptiṅantaṃ padam'. Paraphrase agrees.", "by": "sourcing:U02-brahmana-vedanga"}]}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:astadhyayi:1.4.54", "source": "src:astadhyayi", "location": {"ref": "1.4.54"}, "paraphrase": "The independent one (svatantra) is the agent (kartṛ).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:karaka"], "notes": "The grammarians' and philosophers' reflections on agency (kartṛtva) belong to U31 and other units. Phase-B spot check: wording/locator matched against the local GRETIL/DCS e-text in sources_raw/ (not a formal Phase-C sourcing check).", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-28", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["local text lookup 1.4.54"], "evidence": ["text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/mixed/gretil_devanAgarI/1_sanskr/6_sastra/1_gram/panini_astadhyayi.md (GRETIL)"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "A 1.4.54 'svatantraḥ kartā'. Paraphrase agrees.", "by": "sourcing:U02-brahmana-vedanga"}]}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
